{# Decision template: who the player is addressing, as one choice over the legal (speaker, target)
   pairs the game enumerated. Rendered into a decisions request, never into chat messages.
   Sent when dialogue.decisions.useForPlayerTarget is on; target_selectors/player_dialogue_target_selector
   is the chat fallback.

   Context set by the game: decision_pairs (key, speakerUUID, speakerName, targetKind, targetUUID,
   targetName), decision_speakers (UUID, name, distance, isVirtual, isPrivateVirtual), triggeringEvent
   (the player's line), crosshairTarget, lastSpeaker, lastDialogueTarget, events, maxRecentEvents.
   The speaker of a pair is the NPC who answers; the virtual-NPC rules and no self-target are already
   applied to the pairs. Keys are short and numbered per request (s2_tplayer, s2_t5); use p.key as given.
   There is no none option: someone always answers the player. When the game gets no usable answer, the
   NPC in the crosshair answers, else the nearest one. The crosshair target leads decision_speakers.

   A criterion is one line; profiles and other multi-line decorators belong in the state blocks. #}
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}
{% set lookedAtUUID = 0 %}
{% if crosshairTarget and crosshairTarget.UUID %}
{% set lookedAtUUID = crosshairTarget.UUID %}
{% endif %}

[ state player_line ]
{{ player.name }}: {{ format_event(triggeringEvent, "verbose") }}
[ end state ]

[ state looking_at ]
{% if crosshairTarget and crosshairTarget.UUID and crosshairTarget.UUID != 0 %}
{{ player.name }} is looking directly at {{ crosshairTarget.name }} ({{ units_to_meters(crosshairTarget.distance) }}m away), marked [LOOKED AT] in `nearby`.{% if is_unconscious(crosshairTarget.UUID) %} {{ crosshairTarget.name }} is unconscious and cannot reply.{% endif %}
{% else %}
{{ player.name }} is not looking at anyone in particular.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state location ]
{{ location }}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_dialogue ]
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}
[ end state ]

[ state last_exchange ]
{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} was speaking to {% if lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}.
{% else if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} made a general comment with no specific target.
{% else %}
No one has spoken yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state nearby ]
{% for c in decision_speakers %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(c.UUID) %}
{{ cinfo.name }}{% if lookedAtUUID != 0 and c.UUID == lookedAtUUID %} [LOOKED AT]{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %}{% if c.isPrivateVirtual %} (virtual: a voice only {{ player.name }} hears){% else %} (virtual: heard by everyone here, but not physically present){% endif %}{% else %} ({{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(c.distance) }}m away){% endif %}{% if tagCompanion and is_follower(c.UUID) %} [COMPANION]{% endif %}{% if tagEngaged and is_in_package(c.UUID, "SkyrimNet_PlayerFollowPackage") %} [ENGAGED]{% endif %}{% if tagInScene and ((is_plugin_loaded("SexLab.esm") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction")) or (is_plugin_loaded("OStim.esp") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction"))) %} [IN SCENE]{% endif %}
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if tagCompanion or tagEngaged or tagInScene %}
Tags: {% if tagCompanion %}[COMPANION] travels with {{ player.name }}. {% endif %}{% if tagEngaged %}[ENGAGED] is already in conversation with the player. {% endif %}{% if tagInScene %}[IN SCENE] is physically occupied in an intimate scene. {% endif %}
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question target choice ]
Decide who {{ player.name }} is speaking to in `player_line`, and so who answers. Each option names the person addressed and who they then speak to.
`looking_at` is who {{ player.name }} is facing, and it is the strongest sign of who is addressed. The person marked [LOOKED AT] answers, even if {{ player.name }} was just talking to someone else, unless the line names or clearly refers to somebody else, or they cannot reply. Turning to look at someone is how {{ player.name }} turns to speak to them.
`recent_dialogue` is the conversation so far, oldest first. `last_exchange` says who was talking to whom a moment ago: when no one is marked [LOOKED AT], a line that continues that exchange (a reply, thanks, an answer to a question, a follow-up) is for the person {{ player.name }} was just dealing with.
`nearby` describes everyone in earshot and how far away they are. A name or clear reference in the line decides it. Otherwise the person marked [LOOKED AT] answers. With no one marked, prefer the person in the ongoing exchange, then the person whose role the line fits, then someone close by over someone far away. A remark plainly meant for the people traveling with {{ player.name }} goes to a companion.
A virtual NPC has no body: choose one only when the line names it or plainly answers what it just said. Having spoken last does not make {{ player.name }}'s next line for it.
Choose an option where the person addressed speaks to another NPC only when {{ player.name }} asks them to talk to, ask or tell that NPC something.
When no one is marked [LOOKED AT], a line with no name in it that follows an exchange is for the person in that exchange. When the line could be for several people, choose the person marked [LOOKED AT], else whoever it most likely addresses.
[ criteria ]
{% for p in decision_pairs %}
{% set pv = false %}{% for s in decision_speakers %}{% if s.UUID == p.speakerUUID and s.isVirtual %}{% set pv = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{{ p.key }}: {% if p.targetKind == "player" %}{{ player.name }} is speaking to {{ p.speakerName }}, who answers {{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ player.name }} is asking {{ p.speakerName }} to speak to {{ p.targetName }}{% endif %}{% if pv %} (right only if the line names {{ p.speakerName }} or plainly answers what {{ p.speakerName }} just said){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
